Command parsing must stay under 1000ms p95 — these shapes are the ones that
went quadratic before (long paths without slashes, repeated `cd` with redirects).
A hook that exceeds its 10s timeout is killed — and a killed hook allows the call.

Gate G9 is on the last column — **the fallback must add less than 50ms p95**.
It is a delta, not an absolute, because most of any absolute figure is the `node` startup
above — a number this tool does not control.
`all-state` (every line a state transition) is adversarial input: recorded, not gated. The
journal only grows through harness commands, so reaching 100,000 transitions means running
100,000 of them — hard to reach in practice, though nothing caps it.
